<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muse Bihi Abdi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1948">1948</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muse Bihi Abdi is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> politician and former air force officer who was president of Somaliland from 2017 to 2024. A commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-national-movement">Somali National Movement</a>, he led the ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kulmiye">Kulmiye</a> party to victory in the 2017 election. His term saw war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ssc-khatumo">SSC-Khatumo</a> forces around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/las-anod">Las Anod</a> in 2023, and he lost the 2024 election to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdirahman-mohamed-abdullahi">Abdirahman Mohamed Abdullahi</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muse-bihi-abdi.jpg" alt="Muse Bihi Abdi" width="320" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SLNTV · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Biixi_(1)_Cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
